@startuml
title PayLink - Sequence Diagram: Refund a Failed Payment
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC

legend top left
  All amounts are Decimal in EGP (never float). Ledger entries are append-only;
  balances are always derived from entries, never stored.
  Yellow notes show the Payment state after each state change.
  Scope: a payment that did not succeed becomes Failed and the Customer's money returns.
endlegend

participant ElectroCo <<external system>>
participant TopUpNet <<external system>>
participant BillerIntegration
participant Reconciliation
participant Scheduler
participant PaymentProcessing
participant AccountsAndWallet
participant AuditLog
participant Notifications
participant "SMS/Push Provider" as Provider <<external system>>
actor Customer

note over PaymentProcessing : Precondition: the Payment is SentToBiller (trigger a) or Unknown (triggers b and c),\nand its funds are Held. The "refused during the call" flow is in Pay a Bill, not here.

== 1. Failure signal: three triggers ==
alt a) TopUpNet calls back "failed" for an accepted top-up
  TopUpNet -> BillerIntegration : callback(reference, "failed", errorCode)
  activate BillerIntegration
  BillerIntegration -> PaymentProcessing : failedEvent(reference, who = TopUpNet callback, why = reason code)
  deactivate BillerIntegration

else b) Scheduler re-queries an Unknown payment (after 1, 5 or 15 minutes)
  Scheduler -> PaymentProcessing : requeryUnknown(reference)
  activate PaymentProcessing
  PaymentProcessing -> BillerIntegration : queryStatus(reference)
  activate BillerIntegration
  BillerIntegration -> ElectroCo : statusInquiry(reference)
  activate ElectroCo
  alt ElectroCo says refused
    ElectroCo --> BillerIntegration : refused (error code)
    deactivate ElectroCo
    BillerIntegration --> PaymentProcessing : refused (failedEvent: who = Scheduler, why = reason code)
    deactivate BillerIntegration
  else no answer within 10 seconds
    BillerIntegration -> BillerIntegration : wait for biller answer (timeout 10 s)
    deactivate ElectroCo
    BillerIntegration --> PaymentProcessing : timeout (no answer)
    deactivate BillerIntegration
  end
  deactivate PaymentProcessing

else c) Nightly Reconciliation: an Unknown payment is not listed in the settlement file
  Scheduler -> Reconciliation : startNightlyReconciliation()
  activate Reconciliation
  note over Reconciliation : ElectroCo sent the settlement file beforehand.\nReconciliation does not call ElectroCo or BillerIntegration.
  Reconciliation -> Reconciliation : read the settlement file from ElectroCo,\ncompare it with PayLink's payments
  Reconciliation -> Reconciliation : record the differences in the reconciliation report
  loop for each Unknown payment NOT listed in the settlement file
    Reconciliation -> PaymentProcessing : failedEvent(reference, who = Reconciliation, why = reason code)
  end
  deactivate Reconciliation
end

alt a failed event reached PaymentProcessing (trigger a, b refused, or c)
  activate PaymentProcessing

  == 2. Guard and transition to Failed ==
  PaymentProcessing -> PaymentProcessing : find Payment by reference, check current state

  alt Payment is already Failed, Refunded or Completed (any state other than SentToBiller or Unknown)
    PaymentProcessing -> PaymentProcessing : refuse the transition, ignore the event
    PaymentProcessing -> AuditLog : writeAuditRecord(IgnoredFailedEvent, who = source system actor, why = reason code)
    activate AuditLog
    AuditLog --> PaymentProcessing : recorded
    deactivate AuditLog
    note over PaymentProcessing : State: unchanged (Failed, Refunded or Completed)\nNo second release, no ledger entry

  else Payment is SentToBiller or Unknown
    PaymentProcessing -> PaymentProcessing : move Payment to Failed (statusReason from reason code)
    note over PaymentProcessing : State: Failed\nSentToBiller -> Failed (trigger a)\nUnknown -> Failed (triggers b and c)

    == 3. Release the hold ==
    PaymentProcessing -> AccountsAndWallet : releaseHold(reference, who, why)
    activate AccountsAndWallet
    AccountsAndWallet -> AccountsAndWallet : append LedgerEntry Release\n(Held -> Available, total)
    AccountsAndWallet -> AuditLog : writeAuditRecord(Release, who = TopUpNet callback, Scheduler or Reconciliation, why = reason code)
    activate AuditLog
    AuditLog --> AccountsAndWallet : recorded
    deactivate AuditLog
    AccountsAndWallet --> PaymentProcessing : hold released
    deactivate AccountsAndWallet
    PaymentProcessing -> PaymentProcessing : move Payment to Refunded
    note over PaymentProcessing : State: Refunded (final)\nFailed -> Refunded

    == 4. Notify the Customer (never changes the payment state) ==
    PaymentProcessing ->> Notifications : notifyOutcome(reference, Refunded, statusReason)
    activate Notifications
    note over Notifications, Provider : Customer only. The Agent is not notified for failures.
    loop up to 3 attempts, stop when delivered
      Notifications ->> Provider : sendSMS and sendPush (message includes statusReason)
      activate Provider
      alt delivered
        Provider ->> Customer : SMS and push
        deactivate Provider
      else delivery fails
        Provider --> Notifications : failure
        deactivate Provider
      end
    end
    opt all 3 attempts failed
      Notifications -> Notifications : mark Notification Undelivered
      note over PaymentProcessing, Notifications : A notification failure never changes the Payment state.
    end
    deactivate Notifications
  end
  deactivate PaymentProcessing

else no failed event: the re-query (trigger b) got no answer
  note over PaymentProcessing : State: Unknown (unchanged)\nThe hold stays, nothing is refunded, no ledger entry.\nUnknown is never refunded automatically.
  note over PaymentProcessing, Scheduler : The Scheduler's next re-query (1, 5, 15 minutes) and the nightly\nReconciliation run outside this diagram.
end

note over PaymentProcessing, AccountsAndWallet : A refund of a Completed payment is a separate Refund request (US-27)\nand is outside this diagram.
@enduml